# Local-only working docs kept out of the published repo (original PRD/design
# notes, internal roadmaps/migration runbooks, WIP handoffs). Retained on disk
# for the author's reference; never published.
scratch/

# Orchestration run-state — local session bookkeeping, not product history.
# Gitignored so the guided loop's single-checkout discard (`git stash -u`) and
# `git add -A` never sweep or commit it, and so it never dirties the tree that
# reconcile inspects (ADR 0009). It persists on local disk across sessions.
.agents/run-state.yaml

# The two files that TRAVEL WITH run-state and must share its treatment exactly
# (ADR 0022, ADR 0019 v3.4): the finding BODIES whose one-line index lives inside
# run-state, and the archived overflow of run-state's `note:`. Both are the cold
# half of a hot/cold split whose hot half is gitignored — so ignoring them is what
# keeps the pair consistent. Ignoring is also what makes them SURVIVE: an untracked
# file is swept by the pause path's `git stash --include-untracked` and shows up in
# the `git status --porcelain` that `reconcile` reads as scratch sitting on the green
# checkpoint (which it then discards). An ignored file is invisible to both, exactly
# like run-state.yaml. Same-machine, same as run-state.
.agents/findings/
.agents/run-state-note-archive.md

# Orchestration run-metrics — the event spine + assembled run packets (ADR 0019
# Tier 1). Local run bookkeeping, NOT product history; gitignored for the same
# ADR 0009 reasons as run-state (the loop's `git add -A` / `git stash -u` must
# never sweep or commit it, and it must not dirty the tree reconcile inspects).
# The assembled run-metrics.json is a portable single file — archive a run by
# copying it out, not by committing this live directory.
.agents/metrics/
.agents/metrics*

# gspec build run-state — transient driver bookkeeping, not product history.
# The adapter reads `.gspec/build/status.json` for the two-drivers interlock
# (ADR 0020 D5) and does so FAIL-SOFT, so its absence is a supported state and
# ignoring it costs nothing. `.gspec/config.json` is NOT ignored: it records the
# install target and is the only in-repo trace that gspec is wired up here.
.gspec/build/

